# Rules for AI coding assistants — JellyFin [PS3]

PS3 homebrew built with PSL1GHT and ps3dev. Read docs/DEVELOPMENT.md first.

## The platform
1. 32-bit big-endian PowerPC (the Cell's PPU), no glibc extensions, no C++
   exceptions or RTTI, no std::filesystem, no new threads or global state
   without a reason.
2. **Never invent a firmware or PSL1GHT API.** `cellAudio*`, `sysModule*`,
   `sys*`, `gcm*`, `vdec*`, `spu*`, `net*`: if the symbol is not in a header
   under `$PSL1GHT/ppu/include` (or already used in this tree), it does not
   exist. Check the header before calling it.
3. Memory is tight (about 20–30 MB free at 1080p). Anything that allocates in
   the player or UI must fail soft and be sized deliberately.

## Building and testing
4. Build with the pinned GCC 7.2 Docker image `jellyfin-ps3-build:2026-07-26`
   only. GCC 13 (newer ps3dev) builds hang the GPU on real hardware.
5. Logic that can run on a PC goes behind a host-testable header with a test
   in `tests/` wired into `tests/Makefile.host`. Delete a test binary (or use
   `make -B`) after changing a header it uses.
6. After changing on-screen text, run `python tools/i18n.py gen` and `check`:
   every string needs all five translations.
7. Check every package with `tools/verify_pkg.py` before it goes near a console.

## Editing
8. Match the file you are editing: brace style, naming, comment density.
9. Do not edit vendored or generated code without being asked:
   `source/audio/mlp/ff/` (FFmpeg), `source/gfx/stb_*.h`, `source/ui/fonts/*.h`,
   `source/audio/dca*/tables_*.h`, `source/i18n/i18n_tables.c` (generated by
   `tools/i18n.py`), `third_party/`.
10. C files in `source/audio/` are C; keep the `extern "C"` boundaries.
11. Byte and bitstream code: explicit about endianness and bounds; assume the
    input is hostile and truncated.
12. Write source changes with an editor tool or a script file, never through
    shell here-docs: escapes like `\n` and `\0` have been turned into real line
    breaks and NUL bytes that way. Scan edited files for stray control
    characters before building.
13. Comments state rules and reasons, not history. Measurements and incidents
    go in `docs/*-notes.md` or the commit message.

## GPU, SPU and renderer work
14. A wrong RSX state, texture bind or SPU DMA wedges the GPU or corrupts the
    heap silently. Treat `source/gfx/rsxutil.cpp`, `source/spu/`,
    `source/ui/render/ui_card_gpu.cpp` and `ui_text_gpu.cpp` as owner-only:
    propose changes, don't make them unasked.
15. SPU kernels follow `source/spu/jf_anim_kernel.h`: header-only, pure C, no
    libm, no PS3 headers, struct-of-arrays, with a host test asserting
    invariants (no NaN, bounded output), not golden values.
16. The wave and particle visuals are original work. Never reproduce Sony's
    XMB geometry, shaders or captured data.

## Publishing
17. Never push, tag or publish a GitHub release unless the owner asks.
    Releases follow docs/DEVELOPMENT.md "Releasing".
